    "text": "Write a plot for a story about two people who swap fingerprints. Include a title wrapped in double angular brackets, i.e. <<title>>. In your response please avoid using commas.\n\n<<The Swap of Hands>>\n\nTwo strangers, Clara and Ethan, meet at a small café on a rainy evening. They are both looking for something lost, and their conversation is brief but meaningful. Clara is searching for her lost ring, and Ethan is looking for his missing wallet. They share a moment of connection, and as they part ways, Clara notices that Ethan has a strange ring on his finger. She asks him about it, and he reveals it was a gift from his sister, who had gone missing a few days ago.\n\nAccident\n\nOne night, while walking home, Clara is involved in a car accident. She is rushed to the hospital, and during the emergency, her fingerprints are taken. Ethan, who was driving, is also taken to the hospital. When they are both in the same room, they realize they have the same fingerprints. The doctors are confused, and the hospital staff is unsure of what to do next.\n\nThe mystery deepens as they begin to notice strange occurrences. Clara starts to feel like she is being watched, and Ethan starts to experience strange dreams. They both start to question their pasts and the events that led to their current situation.\n\nAs the days pass, Clara and Ethan begin to swap fingerprints. They start with small things, like a key or a pen. Over time, they realize that the swap is not just a coincidence. They start to uncover clues that point to a larger mystery involving a missing person and a hidden truth.\n\nIn the end, Clara and Ethan discover that their lives are linked in a way they never expected. They learn that their pasts are intertwined, and that the swap was a way to bring them together. They decide to face the truth and find a way to restore what was lost.",
